WEBVTT

00:01.680 --> 00:03.310
Can you...

00:03.310 --> 00:05.730
be friends with me?

00:06.150 --> 00:07.480
Friends?

00:08.630 --> 00:10.230
You don't want to?

00:10.780 --> 00:11.950
See you.

00:13.050 --> 00:14.280
Yes.

00:34.030 --> 00:35.910
Welcome back, Chihiro.

00:35.910 --> 00:36.720
Did you have fun?

00:38.240 --> 00:40.640
Yes, it was a lot of fun.

00:42.080 --> 00:44.040
Don't force yourself, okay?

00:44.040 --> 00:44.750
And...

00:44.750 --> 00:47.150
And I shouldn't get in too deep.

00:47.630 --> 00:49.060
I shouldn't let myself get in too deep.

00:51.550 --> 00:55.780
Himura-san, would it be bad if I told someone about myself?

00:56.930 --> 01:00.010
If it's something you've decided, I won't object.

01:00.010 --> 01:02.350
As for my personal opinion,

01:02.350 --> 01:03.490
I don't approve.

01:05.140 --> 01:06.500
You're right.

01:07.350 --> 01:09.900
Even if I get into trouble,

01:09.900 --> 01:12.000
I won't be able to regret it.

01:50.650 --> 01:52.070
All right.

01:52.070 --> 01:54.380
Onii-chan, it's morning.

01:57.240 --> 01:58.630
Wake up, Onii-chan.

02:02.660 --> 02:04.850
If you don't wake up, you're going to be late.

02:10.830 --> 02:12.710
Well then, since I've already gone this far,

02:12.710 --> 02:16.360
whatever happens afterwards is your own problem.

02:20.700 --> 02:22.910
I told you to wake up!

02:24.410 --> 02:25.930
That hurts.

02:25.930 --> 02:28.310
Aren't your methods of waking me up getting more and more violent?

02:28.310 --> 02:31.310
Because you're sleeping in later and later.

02:31.310 --> 02:34.940
Since it's bad for your health, didn't I tell you to stop sleeping at your desk?

02:34.940 --> 02:38.420
It can't be helped. Because the deadline is soon, it's a major crisis.

02:38.420 --> 02:40.740
Don't you say it's a crisis every single month?

02:40.740 --> 02:44.550
Work is fine, but your real occupation is being a student.

02:44.550 --> 02:47.060
Being a manga artist is also my occupation.

02:47.060 --> 02:50.370
Quit quibbling, and go wash your face right now.

02:50.390 --> 02:52.940
Otherwise, everyone will find out about your job.

02:52.940 --> 02:53.480
Huh?

03:07.030 --> 03:11.540
Onii-chan, if you don't properly go to school regularly, your attendance record will be really bad.

03:11.540 --> 03:14.170
You're slow, and your grades are poor.

03:14.170 --> 03:18.050
On top of being perverse, you don't have enough days in attendance.

03:18.050 --> 03:22.380
It's like you're saying, "Let me repeat my second year".

03:22.380 --> 03:25.550
Then I might be in the same class as you next year.

03:25.550 --> 03:29.890
I'm telling you to go to school on time so that it won't happen!

03:29.890 --> 03:32.560
I wouldn't go as far as telling you to stop publishing,

03:32.560 --> 03:35.190
but come to school more regularly.

03:36.360 --> 03:38.150
Well, I'll think about it.

03:38.150 --> 03:40.610
Yeah, think about it.

03:41.940 --> 03:44.950
Say, have you been reading my manga lately?

03:44.950 --> 03:47.410
Of course I have.

03:47.410 --> 03:50.120
You rarely tell me about your thoughts on them.

03:50.120 --> 03:54.000
Because it's embarrassing to tell you what I think.

03:54.000 --> 03:58.210
Besides, even if I don't tell you, your readers write you letters, don't they?

03:57.710 --> 04:02.090
The suffix "sensei" is used here as a token of respect for a professional, in this case for a manga artist.

03:58.210 --> 04:00.000
Shindou Nagi-sensei.

04:00.000 --> 04:02.090
Don't call me that outside.

04:02.090 --> 04:03.930
Yes, Onii-chan.

04:03.930 --> 04:05.260
No "Onii-chan" either.

04:08.720 --> 04:10.220
Don't doze off.

04:10.220 --> 04:12.270
Properly listen to what the teacher says.

04:12.270 --> 04:15.140
And if the teacher calls on you, answer clearly in a loud voice.

04:15.140 --> 04:17.110
Are you my guardian?

04:17.690 --> 04:19.570
See you, Hirono-senpai.

04:19.570 --> 04:20.400
Yeah.

04:22.690 --> 04:24.950
You're unusually early, Hirono.

04:24.950 --> 04:26.280
Kyosuke.

04:26.280 --> 04:28.490
Moreover, you came to school with your girlfriend.

04:28.490 --> 04:30.740
I guess you've grown into more of a man.

04:31.240 --> 04:34.080
She's not my girlfriend, and it's none of your business.

04:34.080 --> 04:35.670
Listen, Hirono.

04:35.670 --> 04:40.210
Even if she's not your type, it's important to get along with the girl first.

04:40.210 --> 04:43.090
Among her friends might be a girl that's your type.

04:43.090 --> 04:46.760
And there might be even more of your type among her friends' friends.

04:46.760 --> 04:51.220
Your lack of discrimination towards girls is due to that strategy?

04:51.220 --> 04:53.430
Nah, I'm just a fickle person.

04:53.430 --> 04:56.520
You think something said by someone like that would be persuasive?

04:56.520 --> 04:58.810
So, are you going to class today?

04:58.810 --> 05:02.610
Since I'm already here, I'll just go register my attendance.

05:02.610 --> 05:04.690
Attendance only?

05:08.410 --> 05:11.660
VIOLIN MUSIC CO

05:12.870 --> 05:15.370
VIOLIN MUSIC COLLECTION

05:52.530 --> 05:53.450
I...

05:55.240 --> 05:56.120
always...

05:58.000 --> 06:00.500
have a feeling of loss, as if I'm lacking something.

06:01.080 --> 06:06.010
I always feel like a certain color is missing from the world I see.

06:06.510 --> 06:09.970
But I have no idea what color is missing,

06:09.970 --> 06:12.390
and the more I want to search for the answer, the further away I get.

06:12.800 --> 06:16.100
Impatience is gnawing at my heart bit by bit.

06:20.850 --> 06:22.810
You're quite a reckless person.

06:23.310 --> 06:25.820
I'm an idiot, so I can only see what's in front of me.

06:26.190 --> 06:27.480
You're strong.

06:27.860 --> 06:29.320
That's not true.

06:29.320 --> 06:34.080
I just think that someone whose dream comes true has some kind of responsibility.

06:34.080 --> 06:36.790
Who would that responsibility be for?

06:40.750 --> 06:43.420
For the dreamer, me.

06:48.880 --> 06:50.840
Did I fall asleep?

06:51.630 --> 06:53.640
Are you awake, Hirono-kun?

06:54.300 --> 06:55.140
You...

06:55.430 --> 06:58.310
Morning. I'm Miyamura Miyako.

06:58.310 --> 07:01.270
You're a student at Otowa, eh?

07:01.270 --> 07:03.770
My uniform looks pretty tempting too, doesn't it?

07:03.770 --> 07:06.150
You were totally asleep.

07:06.150 --> 07:08.690
If you sleep in a place like this, you'll catch a cold.

07:08.690 --> 07:10.650
So, why are you here?

07:10.650 --> 07:11.820
Isn't it obvious?

07:12.320 --> 07:15.660
I came to see you.

07:21.790 --> 07:25.000
The text "ordinary people may not enter" is read backwards here.
A reference to the manga "Sayonara Zetsubou Sensei".

07:26.920 --> 07:31.510
If only this car wasn't there, it would be a good shot.

07:31.510 --> 07:33.010
Hey, Kyosuke.

07:33.010 --> 07:33.760
Hmm?

07:34.050 --> 07:36.550
The shots you took are good,

07:36.550 --> 07:38.560
but it's tough to combine them together.

07:38.560 --> 07:39.430
Huh?

07:39.430 --> 07:42.520
The shots require so much attention that they interrupt the flow.

07:42.520 --> 07:45.900
When I took the one-cuts, I put all my soul in it.

07:45.900 --> 07:48.570
You should also give all you've got when editing.

07:48.570 --> 07:50.530
That kind of movie won't win.

07:52.490 --> 07:54.910
If you want to win at the Cinema Festival,

07:54.910 --> 07:58.120
you should cater to widely held interests.

08:00.450 --> 08:05.290
But, among our works, there are lots of fans who like the movies Kyosuke shoots.

08:05.710 --> 08:06.710
President?

08:06.710 --> 08:08.210
Since those are popular,

08:08.210 --> 08:11.760
shouldn't our strategy be to make good use of Kyosuke's movies in our productions?

08:11.760 --> 08:13.970
You're right, but...

08:16.140 --> 08:17.300
Kyosuke?

08:18.300 --> 08:19.810
I'm going to the bathroom.

08:23.640 --> 08:26.310
That's not it.

08:27.650 --> 08:30.320
It's about time for me to retire.

08:33.440 --> 08:36.030
That girl... should be Hiro's...

08:39.870 --> 08:40.620
Incoming Mail

08:39.870 --> 08:40.620
Chihiro

08:40.620 --> 08:42.040
Mail Subject

08:40.620 --> 08:42.040
It's almost time for Renji-kun to come.

08:40.620 --> 08:42.040
I'm going to tell him the truth today.

08:43.040 --> 08:46.120
It's almost time for Renji-kun to come.

08:46.120 --> 08:48.540
I'm going to tell him the truth today.

08:50.250 --> 08:51.550
Chihiro...

08:51.550 --> 08:54.760
Good luck. I am always on your side.

08:57.090 --> 08:58.430
E-mail Menu

08:57.090 --> 08:58.430
Write New Mail

08:57.090 --> 08:58.430
Enter Address

08:57.090 --> 08:58.430
Enter Subject

08:57.090 --> 08:58.430
Enter Text

08:57.090 --> 08:58.430
Add Attachment File

09:01.260 --> 09:04.810
Can I go to your place after my club activities, Onii-chan?

09:06.560 --> 09:09.060
Ah, he has his deadline.

09:09.060 --> 09:10.060
MAIL DELETION

09:09.560 --> 09:10.060
Deleted

09:13.150 --> 09:15.360
But I was really surprised.

09:15.360 --> 09:18.280
That you're in the same school as me.

09:18.280 --> 09:21.070
I don't come to school often.

09:21.070 --> 09:22.700
Ah, me too.

09:22.700 --> 09:26.580
When it comes to school attendance, I'm known as the infamous, class-skipping devil.

09:26.580 --> 09:29.250
That's why we don't know each other.

09:31.460 --> 09:36.340
When I saw you, I was unsure whether I should call out to you or not.

09:36.340 --> 09:37.300
Why?

09:37.300 --> 09:39.630
I needed to be prepared.

09:39.630 --> 09:41.650
I'm a girl, after all.

09:41.650 --> 09:42.970
I don't understand at all.

09:42.970 --> 09:47.480
This is our reunion after just the two of us spent Christmas together.

09:47.480 --> 09:49.650
I want it to be romantic.

09:49.650 --> 09:53.110
We just spent our time in a karaoke bar and a family restaurant till morning.

09:53.110 --> 09:55.530
Moreover, I paid for everything.

09:55.530 --> 09:57.530
By the way, Hirono-kun.

09:57.530 --> 10:01.070
Sorry. To tell you the truth, I saw it.

10:01.530 --> 10:02.910
That note.

10:03.740 --> 10:07.830
Is it possible you have that kind of dream?

10:07.980 --> 10:08.960
Dream?

10:08.960 --> 10:10.420
Don't be shy. Don't be shy.

10:10.420 --> 10:12.640
It's not something embarrassing.

10:12.640 --> 10:15.420
It's good to have a dream. Yeah, yeah.

10:15.670 --> 10:18.920
Rather than dreaming about it, I'm already a manga artist.

10:18.920 --> 10:20.760
A self-proclaimed one? Or an imaginary one?

10:20.760 --> 10:22.140
An active one.

10:22.440 --> 10:25.430
A professional one whose series appear in magazines.

10:25.670 --> 10:26.470
Seriously?

10:26.580 --> 10:27.430
Seriously.

10:27.430 --> 10:29.440
What kind of manga are you drawing?

10:29.440 --> 10:38.320
Shoujo manga are intended to appeal to girls.

10:29.440 --> 10:32.230
Generally speaking, shoujo manga.

10:32.230 --> 10:33.190
Eh?!

10:33.190 --> 10:38.320
Now that you mention it, I see you have a girlish face.

10:38.320 --> 10:39.950
That's what you're surprised about?

10:39.950 --> 10:42.410
Heh, that's amazing of you.

10:42.410 --> 10:45.700
In other words, you already have a job.

10:45.700 --> 10:46.790
Well, yeah.

10:46.790 --> 10:48.790
You're already supporting yourself at such a young age.

10:48.790 --> 10:49.720
Well, yeah.

10:49.720 --> 10:51.320
A dream life living on royalties...

10:51.320 --> 10:53.540
Well... Not that far...

10:53.540 --> 10:55.690
Amazing. A master.

10:55.690 --> 10:57.670
Ah, shut up.

10:57.670 --> 11:02.140
If you have the time to praise others, try to do something to be praised for.

11:02.140 --> 11:03.620
Wah, arrogant.

11:03.620 --> 11:05.440
Take a look at my manga.

11:05.440 --> 11:07.850
There are plenty of lines in there that sound even more arrogant.

11:08.850 --> 11:09.850
Seriously?

11:10.180 --> 11:11.180
Seriously.

11:46.300 --> 11:48.050
From yesterday's me...

11:49.720 --> 11:51.140
To today's me...

12:07.830 --> 12:08.910
Eh?

12:09.870 --> 12:12.290
Chihiro isn't here yet?

12:38.360 --> 12:39.400
Good afternoon.

12:40.650 --> 12:42.900
Ah, good afternoon.

12:42.900 --> 12:44.150
You're late today.

12:47.530 --> 12:51.490
I was reading until afternoon passed. Before I noticed...

12:51.490 --> 12:52.730
What were you reading?

12:52.730 --> 12:55.830
Erm, that's... How should I put it...

12:56.890 --> 12:58.040
It was a boring book.

12:58.580 --> 13:00.880
You were absorbed in a boring book?

13:00.880 --> 13:02.550
Ah, nah.

13:02.550 --> 13:04.220
Rather than absorbed...

13:04.220 --> 13:06.260
Something that you can't tell your friend?

13:06.260 --> 13:08.470
Erm, that...

13:08.470 --> 13:10.760
You're my friend, but...

13:10.760 --> 13:11.430
But?

13:13.270 --> 13:14.310
You're mean.

13:15.650 --> 13:16.840
Okay.

13:16.840 --> 13:21.690
It's okay for me to tell you, but please keep it a secret.

13:21.830 --> 13:22.730
No matter what.

13:24.030 --> 13:25.240
I won't tell anyone, no matter what.

13:27.530 --> 13:30.240
Erm, a-actually...

13:30.240 --> 13:33.200
I wasn't reading a story.

13:33.200 --> 13:34.870
Weren't reading?

13:35.410 --> 13:37.290
Is it possible you were writing one?

13:37.290 --> 13:39.460
You're really mean.

13:40.710 --> 13:42.710
Can you show it to me?

13:42.710 --> 13:44.880
I refuse, no matter what.

13:44.880 --> 13:45.880
I see.

13:46.260 --> 13:50.470
But that's amazing. A story, eh?

13:50.470 --> 13:52.430
That's a really unpleasant reaction.

13:52.430 --> 13:54.100
That's not what I meant.

13:54.100 --> 13:55.060
Just slightly.

13:55.060 --> 13:56.980
It's a slightly unpleasant reaction?

13:56.980 --> 14:00.560
Nah, I was just thinking of trying to write one too.

14:00.560 --> 14:02.610
You're writing one as well?

14:02.610 --> 14:04.150
It was just a thought.

14:04.150 --> 14:06.990
I received a career interest survey at school.

14:06.990 --> 14:09.280
I'm thinking of becoming a novelist.

14:09.280 --> 14:11.070
Really?

14:11.070 --> 14:13.530
I think that's a really good idea.

14:13.530 --> 14:14.410
Honestly?

14:14.410 --> 14:15.450
Yes.

14:15.450 --> 14:19.660
I'm interested to know what kind of story you'd write.

14:19.660 --> 14:21.750
I'm also interested to know what you wrote...

14:21.750 --> 14:23.380
You shouldn't worry about it.

14:23.710 --> 14:25.090
I-I see.

14:25.090 --> 14:27.550
You shouldn't touch it for the rest of your life.

14:27.550 --> 14:30.840
Please keep it a secret even after you pass away or go to hell.

14:30.840 --> 14:31.970
O-Okay.

14:32.390 --> 14:35.390
Does that mean I'm going to hell?

14:35.390 --> 14:37.890
But a career is hard to decide.

14:38.140 --> 14:39.480
Really?

14:39.480 --> 14:40.810
It's not?

14:40.810 --> 14:43.900
I think doing what you like will be the best choice.

14:44.690 --> 14:46.070
You're right.

14:46.070 --> 14:47.860
I was told the same thing.

14:47.970 --> 14:49.490
By whom?

14:49.680 --> 14:50.400
An adult.

14:52.160 --> 14:53.910
What do you want to become?

14:54.070 --> 14:57.120
I have a dream.

14:57.120 --> 14:57.870
A dream?

14:58.500 --> 15:03.210
I don't want to become a novelist. I just want to write stories.

15:03.210 --> 15:07.000
Even if it's just a single story, I want to complete one as my current self.

15:07.340 --> 15:08.300
I see.

15:08.300 --> 15:10.470
I believe you can do it.

15:10.470 --> 15:11.970
Really?

15:11.970 --> 15:13.010
Yeah.

15:13.010 --> 15:15.390
Even though my guarantee is not reliable.

15:15.570 --> 15:17.270
That's not true.

15:17.500 --> 15:19.070
Thank you very much.

15:19.070 --> 15:21.560
I'm happy about what you just said.

15:25.820 --> 15:29.320
I have to start going to school again tomorrow. I don't want to go.

15:29.320 --> 15:31.150
You don't want to go?

15:31.150 --> 15:33.660
It's not like I hate school though.

15:34.530 --> 15:36.620
School, eh?

15:36.620 --> 15:37.910
Ah, sorry.

15:38.240 --> 15:40.020
No, it's okay.

15:40.020 --> 15:43.010
It's fun to hear about school.

15:43.010 --> 15:44.670
Rather, it's fun to hear because I can't go.

15:44.670 --> 15:45.630
I see.

15:45.780 --> 15:49.730
My twin sister always tells me about her school.

15:49.730 --> 15:52.080
If she sounds happy,

15:52.080 --> 15:54.520
I'd be happy after hearing it too.

15:54.520 --> 15:55.430
Twin?

15:55.430 --> 15:58.400
Yes. Her personality is the complete opposite of mine.

15:58.400 --> 16:01.470
Onee-chan is like an animal that would die if it stops moving.

16:04.050 --> 16:05.780
She's a first-year student at Otowa.

16:05.780 --> 16:07.610
Her name is Shindou Kei.

16:08.750 --> 16:11.440
But I won't run into her if she's in junior high.

16:11.630 --> 16:12.980
She's in senior high.

16:12.980 --> 16:13.490
Eh?

16:13.490 --> 16:15.290
You two are twins, right?

16:15.290 --> 16:16.440
Yes.

16:16.440 --> 16:18.490
Erm, that means you're also...

16:18.900 --> 16:20.670
If I went to school,

16:20.670 --> 16:22.450
I'd be a first-year student in senior high.

16:22.870 --> 16:24.960
Ah... I-I see.

16:25.370 --> 16:27.960
Ack, I kept thinking she was younger than me.

16:28.480 --> 16:31.710
Erm, should I call you "Shindou-san" from now on?

16:32.710 --> 16:34.220
"Chihiro" is fine.

16:34.750 --> 16:36.540
Everyone calls me that.

16:36.540 --> 16:39.970
Then can you call me "Renji?"

16:40.180 --> 16:42.110
"Asou-san" doesn't work?

16:42.110 --> 16:43.660
It's not the correct form of address.

16:43.660 --> 16:45.970
Then how about "Renji-san?"

16:45.970 --> 16:48.730
"San" is embarrassing. Use "kun".

16:48.730 --> 16:51.600
I'll be the one who's embarrassed if I address you like that.

16:51.600 --> 16:53.860
Nah, see... as a friend.

16:54.960 --> 16:56.340
Okay.

16:56.340 --> 16:58.870
I'll call you "Renji-kun" from now on.

17:00.870 --> 17:02.580
Renji-kun. Renji-kun.

17:03.260 --> 17:05.250
Renji-kun. Renji-kun.

17:06.960 --> 17:08.210
It feels weird.

17:09.020 --> 17:10.210
Yeah.

17:15.310 --> 17:16.760
I'm going this way.

17:17.240 --> 17:18.460
Really?

17:18.460 --> 17:19.300
See you.

17:19.300 --> 17:21.260
Yes. Goodbye.

17:24.650 --> 17:25.640
Renji-kun!

17:28.240 --> 17:29.100
What is it?

17:29.610 --> 17:31.730
I... I...

17:32.160 --> 17:32.900
Chihiro?

17:34.270 --> 17:37.280
No, it's nothing. Goodbye.

17:38.030 --> 17:38.850
Chihiro!

17:39.050 --> 17:39.810
Yes?

17:40.030 --> 17:41.070
Tomorrow...

17:41.360 --> 17:42.200
Tomorrow?

17:42.200 --> 17:43.950
Let's have fun again tomorrow.

17:43.950 --> 17:46.450
I'll come to the station after school.

17:46.450 --> 17:49.460
Can you make it tomorrow?

17:49.760 --> 17:50.920
I think so.

17:51.710 --> 17:54.170
Okay. I'll see you at the station tomorrow.

17:58.920 --> 18:00.050
So it's you.

18:01.430 --> 18:03.300
The one she met.

18:03.720 --> 18:04.890
Himura-san...

18:06.020 --> 18:09.270
If you want to stay by Chihiro's side, you have to be prepared.

18:16.160 --> 18:17.230
Asou-san...

18:17.740 --> 18:21.030
Renji-kun said to me, "Let's have fun tomorrow".

18:21.030 --> 18:23.240
It's not just a greeting like "see you".

18:23.610 --> 18:25.740
It's a real promise this time.

18:26.250 --> 18:27.870
"See you tomorrow."

18:30.000 --> 18:31.380
I want Chihiro to be happy.

18:30.000 --> 18:31.380
Reply

18:30.000 --> 18:31.380
Transfer

18:30.000 --> 18:31.370
Delete

18:31.380 --> 18:33.380
I want Chihiro to be happy.

18:31.380 --> 18:33.380
Reply

18:31.380 --> 18:33.380
Transfer

18:31.380 --> 18:33.380
Delete

18:34.830 --> 18:36.240
Onee-chan,

18:36.240 --> 18:40.590
I can't imagine "tomorrow" and "happiness".

18:40.590 --> 18:41.680
Will I...

18:41.850 --> 18:45.010
Will I still be here tomorrow?

18:45.010 --> 18:49.100
The story he's reading is a folktale called "Kachikachi Yama".

18:50.690 --> 18:54.060
If you want to stay by Chihiro's side, you have to be prepared.

18:54.710 --> 18:59.190
You wouldn't say "be prepared", or something like that, under normal circumstances.

19:18.500 --> 19:19.880
Good luck. I am always on your side.

19:27.410 --> 19:28.310
Yahoo.

19:31.520 --> 19:33.140
Are you Renji-kun?

19:34.120 --> 19:34.900
Yes.

19:35.360 --> 19:36.480
Good afternoon.

19:36.600 --> 19:37.820
Good afternoon.

19:38.280 --> 19:40.030
What should we do today?

19:40.200 --> 19:41.720
Should we go shopping somewhere?

19:41.720 --> 19:43.960
If it's a place with only a few people...

19:44.830 --> 19:48.780
I don't like going outside or to places with a lot of people.

19:52.680 --> 19:54.430
It's really beautiful.

19:54.430 --> 19:56.890
Yeah. As if it's burning.

19:57.800 --> 19:59.210
Asou Renji-san.

19:59.210 --> 19:59.960
Hmm?

20:00.170 --> 20:03.510
Am I your friend?

20:03.690 --> 20:06.060
Why are you asking me again?

20:06.060 --> 20:08.950
Maybe it doesn't mean anything particularly special to you.

20:08.950 --> 20:13.020
What am I to you, then?

20:13.200 --> 20:15.460
I think I was interested in you from the start.

20:15.460 --> 20:17.700
And then, before long, I couldn't leave you alone, or rather...

20:17.700 --> 20:20.180
Yeah, I'm not worried about you.

20:20.180 --> 20:21.890
I always want to see you.

20:21.890 --> 20:24.160
Like a sister?

20:24.350 --> 20:26.550
It does feel like a sister too.

20:26.550 --> 20:31.270
I also thought that if I had an elder brother, it would be someone like you.

20:31.270 --> 20:32.090
Really?

20:32.090 --> 20:33.080
Yes.

20:33.280 --> 20:35.520
And, erm...

20:35.520 --> 20:36.850
I...

20:36.850 --> 20:37.920
Chihiro.

20:37.920 --> 20:38.590
Yes?

20:38.800 --> 20:39.820
Take a deep breath.

20:40.670 --> 20:45.510
This is a popular practice in Japan that is supposed to help a nervous person calm down.

20:40.840 --> 20:45.470
Write "person" on your palm, and then pretend to eat it.

20:46.250 --> 20:47.070
Yes.

20:47.540 --> 20:51.840
I'm sorry, I was testing you a little.

20:52.790 --> 20:57.900
I wasn't sure emotionally if you were the right one to talk to about this,

20:58.090 --> 20:59.550
but now I know.

20:59.550 --> 21:03.720
You didn't change before, and now.

21:04.100 --> 21:07.310
Erm, you're not a different person, are you?

21:07.350 --> 21:08.160
Eh?

21:08.310 --> 21:10.860
Well, since you have a twin sister,

21:10.860 --> 21:14.430
you're not going to tell me that you switched places with your sister, are you?

21:14.430 --> 21:16.020
You're right.

21:16.020 --> 21:19.440
I guess I can't help being regarded as a different person.

21:20.990 --> 21:22.000
Asou-san.

21:24.890 --> 21:28.350
I have a memory defect.

21:29.030 --> 21:31.260
Memory... defect?

21:31.470 --> 21:32.220
Yes.

21:32.430 --> 21:36.170
My memory doesn't last longer than thirteen hours.

21:37.590 --> 21:42.220
In that sense, yesterday's me and today's me are two different people.

21:42.530 --> 21:46.280
Even if I live past today, I won't become tomorrow's me.

21:46.280 --> 21:48.650
I've always been like this.

21:48.820 --> 21:51.240
And I will always be like this.

21:57.870 --> 22:00.710
Fly high, make it

22:00.710 --> 22:03.960
Get to the new world that I seek

22:04.170 --> 22:10.470
Someday with my little wings

22:10.720 --> 22:16.770
Don't look back to the sorrow I left behind

22:17.100 --> 22:22.940
Here's my real intention I hide

22:23.570 --> 22:29.780
I wish you were here, and so just right by my side

22:29.990 --> 22:36.080
Need to be strong enough to swallow my pride

22:36.290 --> 22:42.000
I have been looking for my own style

22:42.000 --> 22:49.470
Don't give it up, here comes the life

22:52.390 --> 22:55.140
Be alive, take it

22:55.140 --> 22:58.390
Promise to find, yes I will

22:58.680 --> 23:04.860
Shining wings filled with wishes

23:05.150 --> 23:07.940
Fly high, make it

23:07.940 --> 23:11.410
Get to the new world that I seek

23:11.450 --> 23:17.910
Someday, so I believe

23:28.510 --> 23:32.180
My feelings and that person's feelings pass by each other.

23:32.180 --> 23:36.720
Next episode, ef - a tale of memories: Paradox.

23:37.430 --> 23:40.500
Do you have memories you don't want to forget?
